<script setup>defineProps({ model: { type: Object, required: true } });</script>
<template><section class="panel preferences-panel"><button class="settings-toggle" :aria-expanded="model.settingsOpen" @click="model.settingsOpen = !model.settingsOpen">Settings & timer details</button><div v-if="model.settingsOpen" class="settings-content"><div class="setting-row"><div><strong>Daily focus target</strong><p>Choose a realistic goal for today.</p></div><input v-model.number="model.dailyTarget" type="number" min="1" max="12" aria-label="Daily focus target" @change="model.saveDailyTarget" /></div><fieldset class="duration-settings"><legend>Session durations</legend><p>Changes apply to your next session. Reset or choose a mode to use them now.</p><label>Focus <input v-model.number="model.sessionDurations.focus" type="number" min="1" max="120" aria-label="Focus duration in minutes" @change="model.saveSessionDurations" /> min</label><label>Short break <input v-model.number="model.sessionDurations.shortBreak" type="number" min="1" max="60" aria-label="Short break duration in minutes" @change="model.saveSessionDurations" /> min</label><label>Long break <input v-model.number="model.sessionDurations.longBreak" type="number" min="1" max="60" aria-label="Long break duration in minutes" @change="model.saveSessionDurations" /> min</label><button type="button" @click="model.restoreStandardDurations">Restore standard settings</button></fieldset><div class="setting-row"><div><strong>Desktop notifications</strong><p>Status: {{ model.notificationPermission }}</p></div><button v-if="model.notificationPermission === 'default'" @click="model.enableNotifications">Enable notifications</button><span v-else-if="model.notificationPermission === 'granted'" class="setting-status">Enabled</span><span v-else class="setting-status">{{ model.notificationPermission === 'denied' ? 'Blocked in browser' : 'Not supported' }}</span></div><button class="why-toggle" type="button" :aria-expanded="model.evidenceOpen" @click="model.evidenceOpen = !model.evidenceOpen">Why these times?</button><div v-if="model.evidenceOpen" class="evidence-box"><strong>A research-informed starting point—not a biological limit.</strong><p>There is no universal maximum focus time or mandatory break length. Brief breaks reliably help vigor and fatigue, while performance effects depend on the task and break duration.</p><div class="evidence-links"><a href="https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9432722/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Micro-break meta-analysis</a><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/21211793/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Sustained-attention experiment</a></div></div></div></section></template>
